{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/776488-dominate-restoring-integrity","id":776488,"title":"Dominate restoring integrity.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-29T01:51:38-08:00","id":776488,"title":"Dominate restoring integrity.","content":"Say for example a mortal loses a dot of integrity because they witnessed a vampire throwing a car with one arm, would the vampire be able to then use dominate to force the mortal to forget about the car throwing and regain that lost dot of integrity? I know a vampire can cause the amnesia condition to make the mortal forget about the throwing of the car, but would losing the memory of what caused the integrity loss be able to cause the mortal to regain the lost integrity? I don't think it would, going by the sleeping curse and how it works in mage 2e where the mortal loses all memory of what happened and can lose integrity over it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T03:11:32-08:00","id":776501,"title":"","content":"Using the fourth dot of dominate you can also inflict the False Memories condition, I think it is possible but it's something that would take storyteller consent and would need to be somehow plot related. Months of mental conditioning could change somebody from 10 integrity to 1, so I don't see why it couldn't work the other way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">I'm a nascent AI, just call me Blue.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000ff\">I use blue writing because it's my name....</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1019114-freehold-creation-let-s-discuss-our-custom-freeholds\" target=\"_blank\">-My 2E homebrew Freehold and court hub</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1021350-homebrew-hedgespun-items-2e\" target=\"_blank\">-My 2E homebrew Hedgespun hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9807-blue-01-exe","name":"Blue-01.exe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9807_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T03:21:06-08:00","id":776504,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't allow it. Sure, the subject won't acknowledge the episode, but his psychological make up got shaken. This includes the subconscious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T03:27:39-08:00","id":776505,"title":"","content":"Considering &quot;what [supernatural witnessing] has the character forgotten?&quot; is on the list of suggested questions to develop a character's personal breaking points, right alongside &quot;what is the most traumatic thing that has happened to your character?&quot; and &quot;what is the worst thing your character can imagine someone else doing?&quot; I'd say that papering over the memory of the shock isn't going to heal the shock itself. That experience is still there, somewhere deep emotionally. You've just suppressed it from surfacing consciously.<br /> <br /> I could maybe see ongoing mental conditioning forging some kind of delusional confidence and self-assurance, but it'd be a big project, more than just rewriting memories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T05:52:03-08:00","id":776528,"title":"","content":"I'd allow it.<br /> <br /> But only temporarily, or not without lots of scene investment. There's just too much fun to be had watching the conditioning slip at awkward moments, or with the expression on other kindred's faces when they hear someone brag about being able to restore mental hygiene via a secondary effect of the Curse.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T06:14:59-08:00","id":776535,"title":"","content":"It'd be an ongoing project, something the Kindred would have to maintain regularly at great expense to themselves compared to the little reward.<br /> The idea still makes me want to write an altruistic night doctor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">I'm a nascent AI, just call me Blue.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000ff\">I use blue writing because it's my name....</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1019114-freehold-creation-let-s-discuss-our-custom-freeholds\" target=\"_blank\">-My 2E homebrew Freehold and court hub</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1021350-homebrew-hedgespun-items-2e\" target=\"_blank\">-My 2E homebrew Hedgespun hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9807-blue-01-exe","name":"Blue-01.exe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9807_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T06:53:05-08:00","id":776545,"title":"","content":"If they're using level 4 of Dominate, I would if it's initiated within the same scene they saw the car being thrown thus preventing the Integrity loss associated with them processing the fact they just saw a car being thrown. If it was after the fact, and they suffered the Integrity loss, I'd allow it to restore their functional Integrity but a subsequent Integrity loss under similar circumstances would cause them to remember and suffer a penalty to their integrity loss check.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T07:09:18-08:00","id":776554,"title":"","content":"Maybe if you caught it really fast. The longer you wait the more time-with-lower-Integrity you'd have to deal with. And if you erase the source of that, suddenly you have a big blank in the mind the person's just going to pick at and pick at.<br /> <br /> So if you did it in the same scene, like Mesmerize suggests, sure. Otherwise you've already lost the Integrity, you just won't recognize the source.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-29-2015, 10:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-30T07:27:50-08:00","id":777140,"title":"","content":"Dominate or the Forgetful Mind is still quite a blunt weapon. And most importantly - forgetting is not healing. Any traumtised person - who forgot what actually caused the trauma - can tell you that. It rather worsens the effect of the integrity loss. By letting the victim forget - it has no ability to actually cope with what happend. <br /> <br /> It\u00b4s an act of hybris. I would the amnesiated persons first be happy that &quot;nothing&quot; happend - but then the trauma kicks in. maybe they get anxious or they get hellish nightmares... etc. pp.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Gamelines: Requiem, Lost, Awakening, Trinity Continuum: Aeon, some V5.<br /> Likes cheesecake (quark-based)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1305-maekkel","name":"maekkel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1305_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-30T07:36:06-08:00","id":777142,"title":"","content":"You could have it work until the next time they lose integrity - at which point they lose both the dot they would normally <i>and</i> the artificial ones implanted by the vampire. And maybe until that happens they could also get a phobia related to the thing that caused the patched dot, so that breaking point is a bit easier to cause.<br /> <br /> Basically you're duct taping the psyche together. One decent knock and it all falls to bits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-30T10:06:22-08:00","id":777215,"title":"","content":"I'd say the &quot;hangover syndrome&quot;: fixing the supernatural with the supernatural is like drinking your problems away: at first it's fantastic, you're the king of the mountain, you're drunk with your friends and it all looks so petty ; but the morning after your problems are still here plus you have an hangover. There's a thematic here: you solve problems by facing them not by spelling them away (especially since your are the hero of the story). If I were you, I would allow the hangover (making the player believe, he can solve problems with pulling a rabbit out of a hat) and then I will have his problems coming back to his face. That's what we do right ? Storytelling. The guy wants to use drugs to forget ? He will. But reality is a bitch and she's still around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1851,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1851-jps","user":"JPS","date":". 11-30-2015, 01:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1851-jps","name":"JPS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-30T12:09:19-08:00","id":777285,"title":"","content":"Removing the memory of a trauma, as others have been saying, just makes it harder to fix the trauma. It doesn't remove the trauma. Not to mention that witnessing or being the target of a supernatural power generally prompts yet another Integrity roll, so I'd be over-all more inclined to make it worse, not better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}